# Local Secrets — TEMPLATE

> **Copy this file to `SECRETS.md` and fill in the values. `SECRETS.md` is gitignored — it never leaves your machine.**
>
> ```bash
> cp SECRETS.md.example SECRETS.md
> ```
>
> Use this file as your **human-readable** secret bundle (what's where, what's it for, when to rotate). The daemon itself reads from `.env`, not from here — so after you fill this in, mirror the values into `.env` as well.
>
> See `CREDS.md` for what each credential is and where to obtain it.

---

## ClickUp credentials

| Key | Value | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `CLICKUP_API_TOKEN` | `pk_REPLACE_ME` | Personal Settings → Apps → Generate. |
| `CLICKUP_TEAM_ID` | `00000000` | Integer from your workspace URL. |
| `CLICKUP_TEAM_NAME` | `My Workspace` | Display label only. |

## Daemon-internal bearer tokens

| Key | Value | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `STANDALONE_API_TOKEN` | (leave empty for localhost-only) | `openssl rand -hex 32` if exposing beyond localhost. |
| `METRICS_AUTH_TOKEN` | (leave empty for localhost-only) | `openssl rand -hex 32` if exposing `/public/metrics`. |

## Postgres

| Key | Value | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `POSTGRES_USER` | `cup` | Default fine for localhost. |
| `POSTGRES_PASSWORD` | `CHANGE_ME_IF_EXPOSED` | Change before exposing port 5432. |
| `POSTGRES_DB` | `clickup_tracker` | Schema name; rarely changed. |

## Per-project hook secrets (optional manual backup)

The daemon generates one HMAC `hook_secret` per registered project. The `install-git-hook.sh` script caches each one at `~/.config/clickup-tracker/projects/<project-id>.secret` (mode `600`). If you want a manual backup outside that directory, list them here:

| Project ID | Display name | Hook secret | Created |
|---|---|---|---|
| `<uuid>` | `<repo display name>` | `<32-hex bytes>` | `YYYY-MM-DD` |

> **Rotation:** there is no rotate-in-place endpoint in v0.1. To rotate, `DELETE /projects/<id>` (a `pre_remove` backup is taken automatically) then `POST /projects` to re-register.

---

## After you fill this in

1. Mirror the values into `.env`:
   ```bash
   cp .env.example .env   # if not already done
   $EDITOR .env           # paste the same values you just filled in here
   ```
2. Restart the daemon so it picks up the new env:
   ```bash
   docker compose up -d --force-recreate clickup-tracker
   ```
3. Verify: `curl -fsS http://localhost:4020/health` → `200`.

Both this file and `.env` are gitignored. Don't commit either one.
